        "title": "Hosted dev-loop harness now forwards caller auth",
        "summary": "The dev-loop control path now threads the caller's JWT through pause, stop, resume, and status so hosted swarm harnesses accept the request.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Pause, stop, resume, and status handlers now extract the caller's JWT and pass it into control_loop and detached-run lookups, so hosted swarm harnesses receive an authenticated request instead of failing anonymously.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "103f2631ebc56b39284d42e74e3fd80642f63ab5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added a dedicated harness_transport module and a per-run harness_auth_token on run handles, giving the server a single place to attach credentials when talking to remote harnesses.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "103f2631ebc56b39284d42e74e3fd80642f63ab5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
