        "title": "Quieter task completions and Grok 4.5 in the picker",
        "summary": "The notifications hook now debounces task-completed events against the terminal loop event, and Grok 4.5 joins the model catalog with pricing and cache-key support.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Task completion toasts and desktop notifications are held for a short dedupe window and suppressed when the matching task-run LoopEnded event arrives, eliminating the duplicate 'task completed' popups that fired for the same run.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "bbddfd9585f8d09f6f95078bf46ef91d2f8bbb6e"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added Grok 4.5 to the model catalog and pricing tables (input $2 / output $6 per Mtok, with cache read/write rates), including the aura-grok-4-5 alias and xai/grok-4.5 normalization.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "f60b119cf02bde3325d798ceed96d580b896773c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Extended prompt-cache affinity docs and plumbing to cover xAI/Grok alongside OpenAI, so stable cache keys now flow through aura-router for Grok conversations as well.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "f60b119cf02bde3325d798ceed96d580b896773c"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          }
        ]
