        "title": "Aura Web Search ships with tiered quotas and optional BYOK",
        "summary": "Brave-backed web and news search is now available by default via Aura-funded credentials, with per-tier quotas, HTTPS-only billing checks, and an opt-in workspace BYOK path.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Web and news search are now on by default using a platform-funded Brave key held server-side, with per-user tier quotas enforced from z-billing and organization membership checks gating access.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "66b327d4fb25227bd6f0e0ebaaf21361829ebe2d"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Workspaces can still bring their own Brave key: connected org-owned credentials stay encrypted in aura-integrations and bypass the Aura-funded quota, with new test coverage for stale BYOK shadows and exact credential routing.",
